29,2,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
30,2,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
31,2,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
32,2,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
33,2,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
34,2,1,talk,Shizue,,It seems the new joiners learned so much just by overhearing us. But the survey shows everyone is fighting over the windows.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,1,talk,Toshio,,The badge records prove it's unfair; some arrive hours before others. And the shuffles last year were a total mess.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The billing is based on area, not people, so we're paying for empty space. Plus, re-running power costs 6,200 yen per desk.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mio,,The pilot floor takes up to nine minutes just to plug in! And those unplanned shuffles Toshio mentioned? A fortnight of chaos!,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"It's worse than that. The printer area is much louder, and the physio says it takes days to get a chair set right.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"If we lose that spontaneous learning, we lose the heart of the team. We must keep people close.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"But if we have fixed seats, the same people always get the noisy spots or the dark corners.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"Every time we change the layout, we pay that facilities fee. We can't afford to keep moving.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mio,,"Exactly! And if we have to set up our screens every single morning, I'm losing precious time between meetings.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Mio, if we move every day, I'll never get my chair adjusted. My back can't handle ""temporary"" settings.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Shunichi, I understand, but imagine the joy of sitting next to someone different every few months.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"Rotating might solve the fairness issue, but does it solve the ""chaos"" Mio is worried about?","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,Rotating would mean paying the facilities quote over and over again. That's a budget nightmare.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mio,,"I agree with Daisuke. I can't handle the ""half-packed boxes"" phase every few months.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,I'm with Mio. Stability is the only way to ensure the noise and ergonomics are managed.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I see. So we are torn between the need for connection and the need for stability.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"And fairness. We can't just let the ""lucky"" ones keep the windows forever.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,I just want something that doesn't cost us more than we have.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mio,,And something that doesn't waste my mornings!,"{""words"":7,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,"Then we need a solution that balances these, though I lean toward staying put.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,,status,Daisuke,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,,status,Mio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shunichi,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
57,3,,status,Toshio,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
58,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
59,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"We have three options: Free Address, Fixed Desks by Function, or Rotating Blocks. I worry Free Address kills the cohesion.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Free Address is unfair because of the arrival times I found. Rotating Blocks is fairer, but maybe too disruptive.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,Fixed Desks by Function seems the cheapest. No repeated facilities fees and no daily setup time.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Mio,,I hate the idea of Free Address. Nine minutes of plugging in every morning is too much. Fixed is better.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Shunichi,,Fixed Desks is the only way I can keep my workstation ergonomic and avoid the printer noise.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"But Fixed Desks means we only talk to the people in our ""function."" We'll become silos.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Shizue, that's true. Rotating Blocks would let everyone experience the window and the noise equally.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"But @Toshio, the cost of re-running power for every rotation... I can't support that.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Mio,,"And the ""fortnight of interruptions"" during the shift! No way. I vote for Fixed.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Shunichi,,I agree with Mio. The physical cost of Rotating or Free Address is too high for me.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Mio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"If we go with Fixed, can we at least promise to move occasionally by hand?","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"That just brings back the unplanned shuffle chaos. If we can't do Rotating, Fixed is the only stable choice.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I feel safer with Fixed. It's the most predictable for the budget.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Mio,,It's the most predictable for my schedule too.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Shunichi,,It's the only one that protects my health.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"I still miss the idea of variety, but I won't stand in the way of everyone's peace of mind.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I'll accept Fixed if we are transparent about who gets the window seats.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I think we've reached a consensus.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Mio,,Finally! Let's just get it decided.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Shunichi,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
